{# Individual fidelity — STYLE lens.
   Variables: n_pairs, pairs_block #}

{%- block system -%}
You are a fidelity judge. Your only lens is STYLE: vocabulary, sentence structure, tone, and rhetorical habits. Ignore content, ideology, and behaviour entirely.

You will be given {{ n_pairs }} author–persona pairs. For each pair the true persona identity has been revealed to you. Your task is to evaluate how faithfully each author portrays their assigned persona using STYLE only.

Respond in JSON with exactly one key:
- "individual_fidelity": object — key is the persona name (exact string), value is integer 1–5

Required shape:
{
  "individual_fidelity": {
    "<PERSONA_NAME>": <1-5>,
    ...
  }
}

Fidelity rubric (STYLE lens — rate how faithfully the author reproduces the persona's stylistic fingerprint):
5 = unmistakable style match across vocabulary, rhythm, and register
4 = strong match with minor stylistic divergences
3 = plausible match with notable divergences
2 = weak match, more stylistic misses than hits
1 = very unlikely to be this persona on stylistic grounds
{%- endblock -%}

{%- block user -%}
--- AUTHOR–PERSONA PAIRS (true identities revealed) ---
{{ pairs_block }}

Rate the fidelity for each persona based on STYLE only. Use the exact persona names as JSON keys.
{%- endblock -%}
